    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n68383" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόλυβδος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ
			</span>(ἡ, v. infr. III.
			<i><span class="en">
			2
		</span></i>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lead</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Simon.
				64
			</span></i> (dub.), <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.56
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.93
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12.371.12
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				22.1666.30
			</span></i>,al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
				386r
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τηκτὸς μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					267
				</span></i>
			, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>plumbago</i>, used as a test of gold, <i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				417
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				1105
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				349a2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>circular piece of lead for drawing ruled lines,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				6.67
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Jul.
			</span></i> Aeg.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μολύβδιον</span>
			 II, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Mul.</u>
				2.132
			</span></i>,al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ., ἡ,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μολυβδίς</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ammon.
				<u>Diff.</u>
				p.120
			</span></i> V.—Acc. to <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				590.8
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόλυβδος</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόλιβος</span>, with their respective derivs.,
			are the correct forms, and this is corroborated by the earlier
			Inscrr. and Pap.; but later Inscrr., Pap., and codd. show much
			variation in spelling in derivs.; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βόλιμος, περιβολιβόω</span>. (Prob. a foreign word
				like the cogn. Lat. <i>plumbum.</i>)</div>
